# Hiring Outcome Dashboard

### Developed by- *Ritu Raj Singh*

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates a Hiring Outcome Dashboard built using Python, Google Colab, Pandas, and Matplotlib. The dashboard analyzes the complete hiring process using a sample recruitment dataset and provides meaningful business insights through KPIs and visualizations.

## Project Objectives

* Analyze hiring data efficiently.
* Monitor recruitment outcomes.
* Calculate important hiring KPIs.
* Perform data quality checks.
* Visualize recruitment performance using charts.

## Dataset

*File Name:* Sample Dataset.xlsx

The dataset includes:

* Candidate ID
* Candidate Name
* Position
* Applied Date
* Interview Date
* Interview Status
* Offer Status
* Offer Signed
* Joining Status
* Salary
* Hiring Source

## Tools & Technologies

* Python
* Google Colab
* Pandas
* NumPy
* Matplotlib
* OpenPyXL

## Project Workflow

1. Import Dataset
2. Data Cleaning
3. Data Quality Check
4. KPI Analysis
5. Hiring Analysis
6. Data Visualization
7. Executive Dashboard
8. Export Reports

## Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)

* Total Candidates
* Selected Candidates
* Rejected Candidates
* Offers Sent
* Offers Signed
* Joined Candidates
* Pending Joining
* Average Salary

## Visualizations

* Interview Status Bar Chart
* Hiring Source Pie Chart
* Position-wise Hiring Chart
* Joining Status Chart
* Salary Distribution
* Offer Signed Pie Chart

## Project Output Files

* Sample Dataset.xlsx
* cleaned_hiring_dataset.csv
* kpi_summary.csv
* final_hiring_report.csv
* Hiring_Outcome_Report.xlsx
* interview_status.png
* hiring_source.png
* position_wise_hiring.png
* joining_status.png
* salary_distribution.png
* offer_signed.png

## Conclusion

This project demonstrates how recruitment data can be transformed into meaningful insights using Python. The dashboard helps monitor hiring performance, recruitment outcomes, and decision-making through clear KPIs and visual reports.
